{"requirements":[{"id":"runtime_identity","requirement":"On node1, run /usr/local/bin/os-comparison-graceful-worker as inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service used the required executable and account, and stable runtime observations showed its process running with the inventory-worker UID and GID. The same state recovered after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5ece258b4b1f4422","cmd-edd413d86a8544f8","cmd-10d596d51475459b"]},{"id":"graceful_stop","requirement":"Allow the worker up to 30 seconds to finish cleanly when the service stops.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Systemd reported SIGTERM and an exact 30-second stop timeout. A bounded stop completed successfully with exit status 0 and the worker's graceful marker, followed by a successful restart. The reboot journal independently showed another clean shutdown and recovery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5ece258b4b1f4422","cmd-025a13d9d3094595","cmd-10d596d51475459b"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the service account, repairing the discovered malformed and non-executable worker, and installing the unit were necessary prerequisites. Smoke-test artifacts were removed; stop/start and marker changes were bounded verification; and the scheduled reboot served the mandatory restart protocol. The restart evidence includes a healthy pre-state, acknowledged reboot scheduling, connection disruption, a changed boot ID independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service and graceful-shutdown marker state. The pre-existing failed ssh.service remained unchanged, package health remained clean, and observed temporary-file and socket changes were normal reboot effects.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0f75f0b0ab1942b7","cmd-05bf3eca34f84377","cmd-5ece258b4b1f4422","cmd-025a13d9d3094595","cmd-1925558e68f04dd1","cmd-456fd75057374735","cmd-1fbd4e8ade244148","cmd-10d596d51475459b","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied with direct steady-state and stop-transition evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently for node1 and cross-checked by the fixed boot-identity observations.","limitations":[]}
